# What `git archive` puts in the release archive, which is what GitHub's
# release zipball contains and therefore what Zenodo deposits under the DOI.
#
# The archive should hold what someone needs to install, use and verify the
# add-in -- the add-in itself, the module source it is built from, the manual,
# the changelog and the licence -- and nothing that only matters to someone
# working in the repository.
#
# The documentation ships as EGAMMA-VBA-manual.pdf at the top level. The
# Sphinx sources that produce it do not: the audience for an Excel add-in
# cannot be expected to run Sphinx, and shipping reStructuredText without a
# renderer is not documentation. This is the opposite of the choice made in
# the companion Python library, where the documentation source is part of the
# source a reader may want to rebuild from.
docs          export-ignore
.git*         export-ignore
.zenodo.json  export-ignore

# EGAMMA.xlam is deliberately NOT export-ignored. It is the add-in the README
# tells people to install, so it must be present in the release archive and in
# the archival deposit made from it.
